 so this is Tony giving up he  just got crushed by Thanos Thanos  performed the snap and then Tony got  stranded in space he's just run out of  food and he's just run out of water and  he's gonna run out of oxygen and he's  gonna die so he records his final  message to pepper his fiancee and then  he turns it off and accepts his fate so  that's pretty much the first minute of  the trailer and it's supposed to be like  that it's supposed to be heavy it's  supposed to be in  because the last thing that happened was  the snap  The Avengers lost Thanos won so Avengers  infinity war ends with an Avengers end  game starts with the defeat of the  Avengers then of course we have the  Marvel Studios logo and of course it  turns to dust and then we see the Thanos  scarecrow and we actually saw this at  the end of Avengers infinity war and  this is actually sort of a tribute to  the comics because in the Infinity  Gauntlet saga when Thanos is defeated he  goes and becomes farmer Thanos and he  puts his armor on a scarecrow in an  attempt to scare anybody who may come  and then we kind of see fan oohs it  doesn't completely show us Thanos what  it really focuses on here is the  Infinity Gauntlet because if you take a  look at the Infinity Gauntlet you can  notice that it is still damaged from the  snap  we know the gauntlet is permanently  damaged the Russo brothers have said  this themselves they said that there was  a cost to using the Infinity Gauntlet  and performing the snap and it  permanently damaged Thanos and the  Infinity Gauntlet the Russo brothers  have also confirmed that this is in fact  a different planet it's tightened to a  new home for Thanos so Thanos is on a  different planet and he and the Infinity  Gauntlet are permanently damaged right  now then we cut to the Avengers facility  where Black Widow is saying that Thanos  did exactly what he said he was going to  do he wiped out 50 percent of all living  creatures and you can see Natasha sort  of choked up when she says that and you  can see Steve crying because not only  did they just lose people that they  loved but they lost as the Avengers they  weren't able to prevent the snap they  weren't able to prevent half of the  universe being wiped away from existence  and then we have this scene right here  where Bruce Banner is looking at a  holograph screen and it shows missing  persons and you see Scott Lang and you  also see Sheree now you can notice that  those red letters to the bottom right of  each picture says missing this is kind  of interesting because they don't really  know where these heroes are they don't  know where Scott Lang is because he  wasn't in the events of infinity war but  it's really interesting that Sheree is  on there because they were in Wakanda  and she was in Wakanda too and the Russo  brothers at one point in time said that  she did in fact survive the snap  a good majority of the Avengers were in  Wakanda Cherie was helping them they all  met Cherie so did she fall victim to the  snap or did she perhaps run away  somewhere for whatever reason because  the Russo brothers did say that she  survived but that could always change  there was a lot of filming that happened  in between when they said she's survived  and the teaser trailer but then you can  see that her picture actually changes to  Peter Parker it's very curious that they  have Peter Parker up there because this  is clearly a missing Avengers profile  list here but I wasn't exactly sure if  any of the remaining Avengers actually  knew spider-man was Peter Parker clearly  they must have known or somehow found  out because he's there but they  obviously do not know where he is  because he's on their missing persons  list then we see a clip of an empty  Avengers headquarters then we see Thor  because he's back on earth now because  he went and got Stormbreaker came back  fought the Battle of Wakanda almost  killed Thanos and now he's with the rest  of the Avengers so now we hear Steve  Rogers voice in the background saying we  lost all of us and then we have this  scene right here with nebula she's on  the ship with Tony and as you can see  here she kind of enters the room that  Tony's in very slowly very cautiously  and she puts her hand on his shoulder  right as Steve Rogers says we lost  friends now Steve's not on the ship  that's just narration but look at the  way that she moves her hand off of his  shoulder she removes it like he's dead  like he's gone and she enters the room  sort of like she doesn't know if he's  going to be dead or alive so I think  there is a possibility that Tony may  actually die in the beginning of this  movie because nebula is pretty much half  machine Dana's ripped a good majority of  her body parts out and replaced them  with mechanical body parts so she can  most likely survive without oxygen and  without food so this isn't the end for  her it's the end for Tony and then we  get our first look at Ronan and it's  interesting that they show him as Steve  Rogers says we lost family and we lost a  part of ourselves because in the comics  Hawkeye becomes Ronan when Steve Rogers  dies and this tragedy Clint gives up his  Hawkeye persona and becomes Ronan so my  guess is and I've been saying this for a  while in a few different videos is that  Clint's family fell victim to this  they got wiped away and during the  tragedy of losing his family not only  did he lose his family but he did lose a  part of himself and then he picks up the  persona of Ronin so from what we know he  is in Japan trying to infiltrate the  Yakuza and as you can see Natasha is  there she clearly went out looking for  him and it seems like she found him  right as he killed a bunch of people so  as you can see Clint or Ronan is not  playing around in this movie we then cut  to the scene with Black Widow and  Captain America and Steve is staring at  a picture of Peggy and noticed that he's  wearing his uniform from Captain America  the Winter Soldier Natasha says this is  gonna work Steven he says I know it is  because I don't know what I'm gonna do  if it doesn't this could be pointing to  time travel the old picture the old  uniform and the fact that ant-man shows  up in another scene in the trailer  because remember that the sequences that  they show you in the trailer are not  necessarily the sequences that are in  the movie in fact more often than not  they're not they're out of order so  ant-man could have told them about a  time vortex that he discovered inside of  the quantum realm and they could have  decided that that's how they're going to  undo the snap time-travel and look at  how they revealed the title notice how a  bunch of different rocks are being put  back together to make the a and make the  title end game it looks like the logo  and the title were broken were smashed  into pieces and time is being reversed  to have them come back together it  clearly looks like time is rewinding and  it's coming back together and if you  notice there is a circle a ring going  around it and as it comes back together  it's spinning this could perhaps be a  portal entrance to the quantum realm  because again a time vortex was  mentioned inside of the quantum realm in  ant-man  and the wasp and the last time we saw  Scott Lang he was stuck inside of the  quantum realm that's me can you buzz me  in so whether or not he gets out through  a time vortex he definitely knows about  the time vortex and when he goes and  finds Steve and Natasha they'll of  course tell him what happened and  explained that oh snap to him in which  he will probably mention the time vortex  as that's probably going to be their  only option to defeat Thanos is to go  back in time so I really think that  that's what we're seeing here the logo  was shattered and time is being reversed  and that's what makes it come back  together and then in the last scene we  have ant-man arriving to the Avengers  facility  he seems really  really panicked